' Chapter 2/3 (class-stream) — a `.flsh` class declaring a `stream` field
' (`public stream onChanged: <Type>`), reachable from whoever holds the instance. `change(...)`
' emits into its own stream field exactly like a script-level `stream` emits into itself — see
' GRAMMAR.md's "`stream`" section, "Also declarable directly on a `.flsh` class".
class Broadcaster {
  public stream onChanged: string

  public function change(value: string) {
    m.onChanged.emit(value)
  }
}
